<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Revolt</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jacobite rising of 1715</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1715">1715</a>–<a href="/years/1716">1716</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Fifteen, Jacobite rebellion of 1715</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Jacobite rising of 1715 was an attempt by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/james-francis-edward-stuart">James Francis Edward Stuart</a>, the Old Pretender, to take the British throne from George I. The Earl of Mar raised the Jacobite standard in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a>, but the indecisive <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-sheriffmuir">Battle of Sheriffmuir</a> and the surrender at Preston in November 1715 ended its momentum. James arrived too late and left for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> in February 1716.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jacobite-rising-of-1715.jpg" alt="Jacobite rising of 1715" width="320" height="156" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: John Wootton · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Battle_of_Sherrifmuir.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
